---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "Schengen Visa for Pakistanis: Destination, Documents & Days",
  "description": "Choose the responsible Schengen consulate from a genuine itinerary, prepare consistent evidence and understand fees and short-stay limits.",
  "intro": "Choose the responsible Schengen consulate from a genuine itinerary, prepare consistent evidence and understand fees and short-stay limits.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "European Commission application guidance",
      "url": "https://home-affairs.ec.europa.eu/policies/schengen/visa-policy/applying-schengen-visa_en"
    },
    {
      "title": "Official short-stay calculator",
      "url": "https://home-affairs.ec.europa.eu/policies/schengen/visa-policy/short-stay-calculator_en"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Use the correct consulate",
      "paragraphs": [
        "For multiple destinations, apply to the country of the longest stay; with equal stays, use the first country visited. Normally the responsible consulate is determined by legal residence. Unsupported “easy embassy” rankings are not a reason to change the stated itinerary."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check consistency before submission",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Follow the consulate’s checklist for passport, photo, application, insurance and supporting evidence. Explain purpose, accommodation, funding and return plans. There is no universal bank-balance figure for every traveller.",
        "Put each overnight stay in order, then compare accommodation, transport and insurance dates. Reassess the responsible consulate if the longest stay changes. Do not submit false bookings or move a paper itinerary simply to seek a supposedly easier authority."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fees and timing",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The standard adult fee is EUR 90 and the reduced fee for children aged six to under twelve is EUR 45, subject to applicable exemptions. Service fees may be additional. Normal decision time is 15 days and may extend to 45; appointment and passport-return waits are separate."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read the visa and count days",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Short stays are limited to up to 90 days in any rolling 180-day period. Entry and exit days count. Your visa may permit less time or fewer entries; unused calculator days do not override those conditions. Use the official calculator to cross-check plans."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "If refused",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Read the refusal form and country-specific appeal instructions. There is no universal A-to-I code list or shared appeal deadline. A new application should address the actual reasons and the genuine trip, rather than relying on another embassy’s supposed approval record."
      ],
      "source": 0
    }
  ]
};
---
<GuideLayout {...guide} />
